(4716896, 677762, 49643, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by CarpeLumen:</b></div><hr/><i> Editing involves rotating, cropping, selective color,Levels, Hue/sat, Curves, selective color, resize, USM, <b>Gaussian blur, faded blur,</b> selective color ,USM framed &amp; saved for web.<br/>this should be Disqualified for sure </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Without violating basic editing rules Gaussian blur can be applied &amp; faded through edit menu. For fading by this method you don''t have to be a image data in adjustment layer.Hope this helps to you.For your kind information I have ribboned in previous soft focus challenge <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=589950" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Soft Focus III</a> by using same method.The top 5 entries are validated on this site, which reconfirms the editing procedure.</td>', 'Originally posted by CarpeLumen: Editing involves rotating, cropping, selective color,Levels, Hue/sat, Curves, selective color, resize, USM, Gaussian blur, faded blur, selective color ,USM framed & saved for web.this should be Disqualified for sure  Without violating basic editing rules Gaussian blur can be applied & faded through edit menu. For fading by this method you don''t have to be a image data in adjustment layer.Hope this helps to you.For your kind information I have ribboned in previous soft focus challenge Soft Focus III by using same method.The top 5 entries are validated on this site, which reconfirms the editing procedure.', '2008-05-22 03:06:12.000000', NULL, 0),
